# UNC-Wisconsin Rhesus Macaque Neurodevelopment Database

Longitudinal structural MRI (T1w, T2w) and diffusion MRI of a cohort of
healthy rhesus macaques (Macaca mulatta), scanned from a few weeks of age
up to 3 years. The database was created by the Harlow Primate Lab
(University of Wisconsin-Madison) and the Neuro Image Research and
Analysis Laboratories (UNC Chapel Hill), with funding from NIH project
5R01MH091645.

This BIDS version was generated by brainspresso from the original NRRD
files hosted on https://data.kitware.com (collection "UNC-Wisconsin
Neurodevelopment Rhesus Database"):

* `sub-<id>/ses-<age>months/anat/*_T1w.nii.gz`, `*_T2w.nii.gz`:
  structural images in the original scanner space (`sMRI/ORIG`);
* `sub-<id>/ses-<age>months/dwi/*_dwi.nii.gz` (+ `.bval`, `.bvec`):
  raw diffusion-weighted images (`DTI/ORIG`). b-values and b-vectors are
  computed from the NRRD gradient table (FSL convention);
* `participants.tsv`: species, sex and date of birth;
* `sub-<id>/sub-<id>_sessions.tsv`: scan date, age (months) and weight.

Questions about the dataset should be directed to the forum of the NITRC
project page: https://www.nitrc.org/projects/uncuw_macdevmri/

## Citation

When using this data, please cite:
The UNC-Wisconsin Rhesus Macaque Neurodevelopment Database: A Structural
MRI and DTI Database of Early Postnatal Development. Frontiers in
Neuroscience, 2017. https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2017.00029
